<title>USA: Rain and snow slow end of Iowa corn harvest.</title>
<headline>Rain and snow slow end of Iowa corn harvest.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES, Iowa 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iowa farmers were busy finishing fall harvest and other fieldwork before the rains and snow hit later in the week ended November 24, according to the state's Iowa Agricultural Statistics Service.</p>
<p>The wintry weather brought fieldwork to a halt, especially in northern areas, the report said. An average of 2.6 days were suitable for fieldwork.</p>
<p>Corn harvest was at 95 percent complete, below the 100 percent a year ago, but slightly above the 94 percent average.</p>
<p>Fall tillage for the 1997 row crop acreage was 41 percent complete. Last year, producers had tilled 48 percent of the intended 1996 row crop acres.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720</p>
</text>
